#: .\templates\index_partials\_about_us.html:15
msgid ""
"The origins of music lie in humanity's desire to communicate with the "
"divine. In ancient times, instruments made from natural materials were used "
"in religious rituals. In Anatolia, religious music that began in Göbeklitepe "
"evolved further with the arrival of the Turks and the spread of Islam. In "
"the 13th and 14th centuries, thinkers like Yunus Emre, Hacı Bektaş Veli, and "
"Mevlana Rumi spread their teachings through music and poetry. After "
"Mevlana's death, the Mevlevi Order was established, and music played an "
"important role in transmitting Mevlevi teachings."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\index_partials\_about_us.html:16
msgid ""
"Mevlevi lodges became centers for art education, elevating music to "
"professional levels. The Mevlevi Ceremonies, as the most magnificent form of "
"Sufi music, created a rich musical heritage and allowed the integration of "
"Turkish musical instruments. Classical Turkish Music, enriched by Mevlevi "
"Ceremonies, gained significant recognition in world music. The Sufi Meshk "
"Ensemble continues to preserve and honor this heritage, working to "
"standardize the Mevlevi Ceremonies."
msgstr ""

